### Rank & XP ladder + offline standing (2026-06-11) — the "You" hub redesign

The profile was rebuilt around a **game layer**, all derived from existing finished-session data
(**no DB migration**; avatar is an app-private file). Pure engines live in `domain/rank/` (the
TrophyEvaluator pattern); `data/repo/ProfileRepository` assembles one snapshot + runs them (the
`AdaptationRepository.engineStatsRead()` fan-out pattern); `ProfileViewModel` is now a thin mapper.
The old header line "Level {trophy points}" is replaced by the rank ladder.
- **XP** (`XpEngine`) — earned, not just trophy points: finish a workout **+100**, each set **+4**,
  each PR **+50**, every 1,000 lb **+5**, each active week **+40**, plus trophy tier points. Returns a
  per-source `XpBreakdown` (drives the "How XP works" sheet). Weights are constants in one place.
- **Rank ladder** (`RankLadder`) — 6 forge tiers (Ember → Iron → Steel → Tempered → Forged →
  Damascus) × 5 sub-ranks (I–V) = **30 ranks**; `rankFor(xp)` → `RankInfo` (tier, "Iron IV", XP into
  rank, XP-to-next-tier, progress, isMax). All thresholds in `TIER_FLOOR` (Damascus open-ended via a
  fixed sub-step); calibrated so ~85 sessions / ~400k lb lands in Tempered.
- **Standing** (`StandingEngine`) — the leaderboard the app can't really have (offline/single-user):
  consistency (sessions/wk), streak weeks and weekly volume over 90 days are mapped through a
  documented population model to a "Top X%" band, honestly labelled an estimate vs typical lifters.
- **Signature** — top lift (heaviest set ever, `LoggedSetDao.topLift()` + `Program.exercise(id).name`),
  most-logged day, usual hour (modal session hour).
- **UI** (`ui/profile/`, split per no-monolith): `RankSection` (6-node track w/ tier icons + XP-to-next
  + tap → `RankInfoSheet`), `ProfileLedger` (ledger/standing/signature), `ProfileExtras` (mirror-test
  photos, trophy-case icon grid w/ progress rings, on-the-record recaps), avatar via Photo Picker
  (`AvatarRepository`). Reuses `TrophyIconBadge`, `bounceClick`, `ProgressPhotoImage`.
- Tests: `domain/rank/` — `RankLadderTest` (boundaries, sub-rank romans, Damascus cap, monotonicity),
  `XpEngineTest` (per-source weights, the Tempered calibration), `StandingEngineTest` (monotonic,
  clamp, interpolation). JVM suite green; `compileDebugKotlin` clean. **Pending:** on-device check.
- **Hero-emblem redesign (2026-06-14):** `RankSection` reworked from the cramped 6-node track into a
  big **hero emblem** for the current tier (glow + tier ring) over a **slim six-dot rail** where the
  connector lives only in the gaps (no longer slices through the emblems) and every dot wears its own
  `RankTier.colorArgb`. Ember/Flare now render a **custom Canvas fire** (`RankEmblem.kt`: 3 stacked
  flame paths + rising embers, out-of-phase oscillators read at draw time) so the flames themselves
  lick/flicker instead of the whole glyph swaying; other tiers keep their animated Material glyph as a
  hero fallback until they get bespoke drawings. Reduced-motion honoured (still flame). `compileDebugKotlin`
  clean; **pending:** on-device check + custom drawings for Nova/Pulsar/Quasar/Supernova.

