## Gym — Active Workout (Day Screen)

### Warmup Gate
- 4 warmup items per day (day-specific exercises/stretches)
- Checkbox list — auto-advances when all ticked
- "Skip warmup" button
- Gate disappears on completion, exercise list appears

### Session Management
- Session persists to DB on start (survives app kill / rotation)
- Active session rehydrates on screen re-entry
- **Leave-session dialog** (`LeaveSessionDialog`, shown on back when sets exist): **Resume later** (keeps the session active and pops back — logged sets persist, reopening the day resumes it), **Discard** (drops the session), or **Keep going**
- **Cross-day guard** (`CrossDaySessionDialog`): opening a day while a *different* day's workout is still in progress prompts "Resume {other day}" (go back) or "Discard & start {this day}" — only one session is active at a time, so it never silently resumes the wrong day
- **Per-sitting active timing (2026-06-11, DB v19→20):** a workout trained across "resume later" sittings now sums its real ACTIVE time instead of the clock resetting each open. New `session_segment` table (one row per sitting, start/end; cascades on session delete) + denormalized `session.active_seconds` stamped at finish. `beginSessionForThisDay` closes any dangling segment (process-death best-effort = last in-segment set time) and opens a fresh one; leave-and-resume / finish close it; `finishSession` returns the summed active seconds, used for the summary duration. Live readout anchored via `DayUiState.elapsedAnchorMs` (= now − prior-sittings ms) so `LastSessionStrip` shows the running total; the date pill keeps the real first-start. Exports list the per-sitting breakdown; `InsightEngine` estimate-calibration + PDF/JSON read `active_seconds` (fall back to wall-clock for pre-feature rows).
- "Quick start" nav arg (skipWarmup=true) skips warmup gate entirely
- **Program-change guard (0.8, `ProgramChangeGuard` Singleton + `ProgramChangeGuardHost` at app root):** generating, deloading, or re-rolling the program while a session is in progress pops a confirmation showing how many logged sets would be lost, instead of silently discarding them

### Exercise List
- **Orphan fix (2026-06-11):** opening a finished/skipped exercise that sits *later* in the list no longer hides incomplete ones before it. UP NEXT (`DaySessionContent`) now lists every remaining-work exercise (not just those forward of the shown index), ordered next-after-current then earlier — so nothing vanishes from the view (the data was always intact; resume rebuilt it).
- Collapsible exercise cards (tap to expand/collapse)
- Previous session "last time" text shown per exercise (e.g. "Last: 30 lb × 10")
- Weight prefill from last session
- **DONE / SKIPPED section (0.6):** completed/skipped exercises collapse into a list below the current one (keyed by position to allow the same exercise twice), still tappable to re-open and edit; **skipping an exercise auto-advances** focus to the next incomplete one

### Beat the ghost (2026-06-11 — engagement)
Every set is framed as a duel with last session, building on the existing per-set comparison
(green Δ-vs-last in `SetRow`, ghost prior shown, gold PRs):
- **Live scoreboard** in the session hero (`DaySessionContent`): "⚡ BEATING LAST SESSION · N/M
  sets" (green when winning), from `DayUiState.ghostBeats`/`ghostComparable` (pure computed props
  over each logged set vs the same-position prior set; `beatsPriorSet` = heavier, or equal weight
  for more reps, or more volume / more bodyweight reps).
- **"beat 45×10"** target on the active input row (`SetInputRow`, was "try …"; still tap-to-fill).
- **Duel result** in the session summary ("Beat last session on N of M sets" / "Clean sweep");
  finishing fires **confetti** for a trophy, a best-ever session, OR a clean sweep — finishing is
  now an event (`SessionSummarySheet`, `SessionSummary.ghostBeats/ghostComparable`).
- **Streak hook** on Overview: a "🔥 N-day streak — keep it alive" line under the week strip
  (≥2 days; the underlying streak is vacation-aware + gap-bridged, so it's encouraging not guilt-y).

### Set Logging
- Weight + reps input row per set
- Forgiving input parser: "45x10" in the weight field auto-fills both weight and reps
- PR badge shown inline on set rows where a PR is detected in real time
- PR detection: compares max weight against all historical sets for that exercise
- Long-press any logged set row → instantly logs identical weight + reps as the next set
- "Use last: X lb" chip pre-fills weight from previous session when field is blank
- Weight suggestion chip ("Try: X lb · reason") shown when auto-progression or effort rating triggers a change; one tap applies it
- **Input modes per exercise unit (0.6):** bodyweight exercises show "BODYWEIGHT / BW" and log reps only; cable/machine (PLATES) exercises log a **plate count** ("PLATES", with the lb equivalent shown), using a **configurable plate weight** (Settings → Equipment / onboarding: 5/10/15/20/25/45 lb)
- **Reps pre-fill** the top of the target rep range and reset to it after each set; weight + reps also seed from your previous session's set at the same position
- **Δ-vs-last column** always fills (extra "bonus" sets compare against last session's final set; "+0" on an exact match; plate exercises show the delta in plate counts) and the **PR ★ marks the actual record-setting set**, not always set 1

