  proposed → applied | skipped; applied → reverted.
- **Planner upgrades** (`AutoCoachPlanner.evaluate(s, CoachPassInputs)`): coach-locked slots
  (any user customization → untouchable, hardening 9); swap proposals carry a concrete
  replacement ("Rotate DB Row → Seated Low Row", payload = lib id from the slot's pre-filtered
  candidates); **volume ±1** — +1 set to ONE muscle only when all its tracked lifts progress,
  fatigue is Fresh, last week hit the session target, the muscle isn't inside an outcome window,
  and net coach drift stays within ±2 sets (hardening 11); −1 set from an exercise skipped ≥3 of
  its last 4 bouts. Priorities: deload ⊃ all → reverts → swap → rep-shift → volume; beginner cap
  1/week. Weight nudges dropped from the Brief (the chip + coach feed deliver them live).
- **`OutcomeWatcher`** (pure): judges applied changes — swap/rep-shift failed if the exercise
  got skipped ≥2× since apply; volume_up failed if fatigue crossed into deload territory;
  conservative types pass when the 14-day window closes. Failed → revert proposal in the next
  Brief; user undo records failed directly. Outcomes feed Phase 4's per-type trust math.
- **`CoachRepository` apply path** — every write is an existing user path (hardening 8):
  swap → `CustomizationRepository.setSwap`; rep-shift/volume → `ProgramCustomizationRepository`
  rep/sets overrides; deload → existing `applyDeloadWeek` (the one non-undoable apply); revert →
  per-change undo of the original. `applyDecision`/`skipDecision`/`undoDecision`/`applyAll`;
  before-state recorded at apply; coach-locked scan = all customizations minus coach-touched
  targets (a coach swap must not self-lock).
- **Brief UI**: proposed rows get Apply→/skip, applied rows show "applied ✓ · undo" (undo hidden
  when not mechanically undoable), reverted/skipped rows muted; "Apply all (N) →" when >1 open;
  disclaimer flips to "Proposals — nothing changes until you apply it."
- Tests: planner 13 (locks, volume gates, drift cap, outcome-window lock, revert priority) +
  watcher 6. Suite green.

**Phase 4 — Autopilot (earned auto-apply), shipped (2026-06-10; JVM-tested, device pending).
🎯 ALL 5 auto-coach phases are now built.**
- **`TrustLedger`** (pure): per-type accepted streak walking newest→oldest — applied extends,
  skip/revert breaks, a failed watcher outcome resets to zero (demotion). Tiered by blast radius
  (hardening 2+3): rep-shifts/removed-sets earn at 3 consecutive accepts, swaps/added-sets at 4;
  **deload and revert never auto-apply**. Undecided proposals count neither way.
- **`COACH_MODE` pref** ("suggest" default | "auto"): in auto, `ensureWeeklyPass` auto-applies
  fresh decisions whose type earned trust (judged on history EXCLUDING the new week); everything
  else still proposes. No-auto-on-error holds by construction (errored passes have no decisions).
- **Settings → Program → Coach page**: Suggest / "Earn auto-apply" chips (honest copy: a type
  must be accepted 3–4 weeks running, one bad outcome demotes, deloads always ask), per-type
  earned-trust readout ("2/4 accepted" → "auto ✓"), and **Coach history** — every pass incl.
  holds, with per-decision status and undo for applied changes.
- The Overview "NEW BRIEF" banner (see Phase 1 entry points) summarizes the pass outcome
  ("N proposal(s)" / "N change(s) applied" / "holding steady" / "couldn't run") via
  `CoachRepository.summaryFor`.
- Tests: 9 TrustLedger.

**Refresh ties into coach data (2026-06-10, post-Phase-4):** regeneration used to silently
discard the coach's applied changes (the overlay reconcile clears them — correct for stale
bindings, but it forgot months of learning on every re-roll). Now every generate/re-roll path
(`ProgramRepository.generate` + `rerollDay`, so Settings generate, deload, manual + auto
rotation all inherit it) enriches its params from the coach record via pure
`domain/coach/CoachGenBias`:
- **volumeBias** — net still-APPLIED volume_up/volume_down per muscle (reverted/skipped drop
  out), clamped ±2 (the drift cap) → `GenerationParams.volumeBias` →
  `VolumeModel.allocate(bias)`: each +1 lands on the muscle's smallest slot, each −1 off its
  largest, BEFORE the weekly cap (junk-volume guard still wins).
- **prefer** — swap replacements the watcher judged "ok" → unioned into `liked` (boosted).
- **avoid** — failed swap replacements → `GenerationParams.avoid`, soft ×0.2 selection penalty
  (a later "ok" on the same movement outranks an earlier failure).
Recomputed from the same rows on every call → idempotent, never compounds; empty history =
exactly the un-coached generator. Tests: 7 CoachGenBias + 3 VolumeModel bias + 2 generator
(avoid steering, bias flow-through).

